File Index

/contribute.md
Purpose: Enables players to submit item and creature data to the Shattered Archive project.

/questbot.md
Purpose: Automates DSL quest cycles with combat resume, egg management, and stats tracking.

/user-equipment.md
Purpose: Tracks character equipment through authoritative snapshots and optimistic live updates.

/library-sync.md
Purpose: Player-facing guide to Library cloud sync (parchment/notes/books) across web, mobile,
and the shatteredarchive.com "My Writings" page — manual Save/Load that merges rather than
replaces, plus a plain-English explanation of per-account encryption at rest. Companion to
scripting-and-sharing.md, which covers scripts/plugins (full replace, not merge).

/organizations.md
Purpose: Player-facing guide to Organizations (kingdoms/clans/religions/friend groups) —
playing as a character rather than your login, one-org-per-category with auto-leave on a
same-category move, account-level admin roles for cross-org access, character-scoped
roles (Leader/Moderator/Member), invites vs. join requests, the leave/remove/ban
distinction (ban = account-wide, reason-required, mod/leader-only visibility), shared
org content (parchment/notes/books in up to 5-level folders), and per-organization
envelope-key encryption with rotation on any access loss, the per-org audit log, and
append-only content revision history with web-only revert. Phase 2 is now fully
COMPLETE (all 7 steps, live-verified end to end across web, game-client, and mobile)
— org management (create/invite/roles/bans) plus revision history/audit stay
website-only by design; browsing and role-gated editing of shared content works on
all three clients.

/user-library.md
Purpose: This file documents the structure, functionality, and developer guidelines for the LibraryModal component in a React-based writing tool. Now also covers tag-based grouping, line/char-limit warnings, and the optional cloud-sync layer (librarySync.ts) — see library-sync.md for the player-facing version.
